/**
\mainpage cognexDataMan100 EPICS Support Module
\section intro_sec Introduction
Support for cognex's data man 100 bar code reader.\n

The DataMan 100 when configured to use its serial port and triggered outputs over the serial line the code read from the bar code.

Documentation of the DataMan 100 at cognex's website: 
http://www.cognex.com/products/barcode-readers-scanners/dataman-100-200-barcode-decoder/

The device supports various types of bar codes.

The intention is to use the device for data matrix codes placed on pins.
QR codes and micro QR codes are also possible.

The device is configured using its USB port connected to the DM100 IOBOX.
Once configured, it can operate stand-alone.

Possible triggering modes are:
- manual using the button on the camera
- external, using the trigger input (input 0). An 24 V pulse triggers the barcode scanning.
- Self (internal)
- Burst (gated).

Serial parameters can be configured on the device as described in the manual.

\section release_notes Release Notes
Release 1 - Nov 2016
Tested with Beamline I11's terminal server and using a serial line.

**/

